WEBVTT

00:00:03.430 --> 00:00:05.440
Oh, Minamikujou!

00:00:06.050 --> 00:00:08.650
Crap, delete!

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:07.060
Delete

00:00:07.060 --> 00:00:08.640
Delete Photo

00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:14.360
That's a pretty good crowd!

00:00:15.050 --> 00:00:17.910
Wow, Mikage!

00:00:22.760 --> 00:00:24.840
<i>Damn visitor!</i>

00:00:24.840 --> 00:00:29.130
<i>Don't be so smug just because you 
got to smile in a photo with Mikage!</i>

00:00:29.460 --> 00:00:30.340
Delete!

00:00:30.340 --> 00:00:34.350
Hey, quit deleting photos I took.

00:00:34.350 --> 00:00:35.630
<i>Come to think of it...</i>

00:00:35.630 --> 00:00:37.850
<i>Mikage promised we'd go have fun somewhere.</i>

00:00:38.180 --> 00:00:42.310
<i>I wonder if she's swept it under 
the rug because of what happened.</i>

00:00:42.310 --> 00:00:44.520
<b>Ooezo Agricultural High School Dormitory for Future Agriculture Managers</b>

00:00:43.450 --> 00:00:46.960
Guys, quit fooling around and go to sleep!

00:00:46.960 --> 00:00:49.990
Okay, good night.

00:00:49.070 --> 00:00:49.990
Mikage...

00:00:51.860 --> 00:00:53.310
I'll go ahead.

00:00:53.310 --> 00:00:54.180
Okay.

00:00:56.160 --> 00:00:59.540
U-U-Um, about that promise...

00:01:00.010 --> 00:01:01.400
Is it still on?

00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:02.640
Promise?

00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:06.630
You know, about u-us going 
somewhere to have fun...

00:01:06.630 --> 00:01:07.560
Oh.

00:01:07.560 --> 00:01:09.840
We talked about going after the festival,

00:01:10.190 --> 00:01:13.260
but because of what happened to me, uh...

00:01:14.630 --> 00:01:17.670
I wondered if it got swept under the rug.

00:01:17.670 --> 00:01:18.980
Not at all.

00:01:18.980 --> 00:01:20.720
I'm really looking forward to it!

00:01:21.800 --> 00:01:24.130
I r-really am.

00:01:24.130 --> 00:01:25.110
Go to sleep.

00:01:26.500 --> 00:01:28.050
Okay, good night!

00:01:28.050 --> 00:01:30.250
Yeah, night!

00:01:34.970 --> 00:01:37.700
Yeah!

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:43.790
Go to sleep, Hachiken.

00:01:45.330 --> 00:01:47.470
You sure you don't need to rest some more?

00:01:47.470 --> 00:01:49.320
I'm all good.

00:01:49.320 --> 00:01:51.300
IVs really work.

00:01:51.300 --> 00:01:53.200
I feel much better.

00:01:53.200 --> 00:01:54.300
You say that,

00:01:54.300 --> 00:01:56.160
but you've still got dark 
circles under your eyes.

00:01:57.570 --> 00:01:59.120
Don't work yourself too hard.

00:01:59.120 --> 00:02:01.300
You need to ask for help when you need it.

00:02:03.560 --> 00:02:05.110
Oh, yeah.

00:02:05.110 --> 00:02:07.570
I'll be sure to take care of myself.

00:02:07.960 --> 00:02:08.930
Thanks.

00:02:08.930 --> 00:02:09.770
No prob.

00:02:10.350 --> 00:02:14.070
<b>Ooezo Agricultural High School Dormitory for Future Agriculture Managers</b>

00:02:10.780 --> 00:02:11.960
Lights out!

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:19.980
You can't even maintain your own health.

00:02:20.450 --> 00:02:22.880
And this is the school you chose?

00:02:24.960 --> 00:02:27.990
I didn't make any comments 
about how it tasted.

00:02:29.290 --> 00:02:31.330
It's okay to run away in order to live.

00:02:31.330 --> 00:02:32.770
It's entirely okay.

00:02:34.820 --> 00:02:36.630
<i>I'm glad I ran here.</i>

00:02:37.610 --> 00:02:39.860
<i>I like this school and my friends.</i>

00:02:40.280 --> 00:02:42.410
<i>I don't regret running anymore.</i>

00:02:43.490 --> 00:02:44.350
<i>But...</i>

00:02:45.840 --> 00:02:47.670
<i>in my case,</i>

00:02:47.670 --> 00:02:51.310
<i>it's not like the problems 
I left behind went away,</i>

00:02:51.470 --> 00:02:52.790
<i>Headmaster...</i>

00:04:24.990 --> 00:04:27.700
Dairy Science

00:04:25.550 --> 00:04:30.520
<b>Fall Chapter Episode 7
Komaba 
Stands on the Pitcher's Mound</b>

00:04:25.640 --> 00:04:28.240
All right. Now that the 
Ezonoo Festival is over,

00:04:28.240 --> 00:04:30.620
life will return to normal.

00:04:30.990 --> 00:04:34.780
Let's all calm down and focus.

00:04:35.610 --> 00:04:39.140
Starting today, the baseball team is away 
in Sapporo for the All-Hokkaido Championships.

00:04:39.140 --> 00:04:40.300
Busy, busy.

00:04:40.300 --> 00:04:43.300
<b>2013 66th Fall Hokkaido High School Baseball Championships</b>

00:04:40.760 --> 00:04:41.920
If they make it to the finals,

00:04:41.920 --> 00:04:43.300
the school will get to go cheer them on.

00:04:44.010 --> 00:04:46.550
If we get to go to Sapporo, 
show us around, Hachiken.

00:04:46.810 --> 00:04:49.890
Sure, but even residential 
areas get brown bears.

00:04:49.890 --> 00:04:50.950
The clock tower!

00:04:50.950 --> 00:04:51.920
Hitsujigaoka!

00:04:51.920 --> 00:04:52.790
Oodoori Park!

00:04:52.790 --> 00:04:55.780
Hey, we wouldn't be going there for fun.

00:04:57.870 --> 00:05:00.910
<i>We will now begin the opening ceremony</i>

00:05:00.910 --> 00:05:05.030
<i>for the Fall Hokkaido District 
High School Baseball Tournament.</i>

00:05:07.520 --> 00:05:09.490
You're going to put the sleds away already?

00:05:09.490 --> 00:05:11.730
Yeah, we have to return them.

00:05:11.730 --> 00:05:13.370
Oh, why aren't you at your club?

00:05:13.370 --> 00:05:16.370
They canceled our club today 
because of morning classes.

00:05:16.780 --> 00:05:18.850
This was really heavy!

00:05:18.850 --> 00:05:19.740
Yeah!

00:05:19.740 --> 00:05:21.020
Hello!

00:05:21.020 --> 00:05:22.440
Hello!

00:05:22.780 --> 00:05:26.510
Nakajima-sensei is having some health issues,

00:05:26.510 --> 00:05:30.620
so I'll be taking care of the 
equestrian club for a while.

00:05:30.620 --> 00:05:31.410
Oops.

00:05:31.410 --> 00:05:33.470
Is he okay?

00:05:33.470 --> 00:05:35.770
So, as for today...

00:05:36.140 --> 00:05:39.860
The horses are tired from the Ezonoo Festival, 
so I'm calling a day off.

00:05:40.770 --> 00:05:44.660
I guess we also have nothing to 
do until evening stable chores.

00:05:44.660 --> 00:05:45.890
Oh, man!

00:05:45.890 --> 00:05:48.080
Now my afternoon's wide open!

00:05:48.400 --> 00:05:51.450
Ookawa-senpai, are you 
really on the job market?

00:05:51.760 --> 00:05:54.450
You still haven't found a job?

00:05:54.930 --> 00:05:55.750
I haven't!

00:05:56.360 --> 00:05:58.580
Why don't you try praying at a shrine?

00:05:58.580 --> 00:06:00.190
Asking for divine intervention, huh?

00:06:00.190 --> 00:06:02.750
What's the largest shrine around here?

00:06:02.750 --> 00:06:05.010
How about the Ooezo Shrine?

00:06:05.310 --> 00:06:08.720
Their prayer ema are shaped 
like a horse. They're cute.

00:06:13.530 --> 00:06:14.550
Mikage...

00:06:15.500 --> 00:06:17.060
Since our afternoon's free...

00:06:17.590 --> 00:06:18.790
want to go to the shrine?

00:06:19.980 --> 00:06:21.020
By ourselves?

00:06:23.470 --> 00:06:27.740
<i>She's probably happy thinking 
about the horse-shaped ema...</i>

00:06:28.760 --> 00:06:30.640
Hachiken's taking off!

00:06:30.640 --> 00:06:32.490
Mikage's stepping out, as well!

00:06:32.490 --> 00:06:34.240
Take care!

00:06:36.210 --> 00:06:37.540
What, what, what?

00:06:37.540 --> 00:06:40.060
Where are you two going?

00:06:40.060 --> 00:06:43.120
I wanna go, too!

00:06:50.690 --> 00:06:52.520
Hachiken, go now! {0651}{Z: HAHAHA}

00:06:53.320 --> 00:06:55.090
Hachiken-kun, let's go!

00:06:59.130 --> 00:07:01.400
What... was that?

00:07:01.400 --> 00:07:05.300
Y-Yeah, I wonder.

00:07:13.470 --> 00:07:15.430
It's nice and quiet.

00:07:15.430 --> 00:07:16.320
What?

00:07:16.320 --> 00:07:19.320
Oh, yeah. It is.

00:07:24.690 --> 00:07:25.990
Um...

00:07:25.990 --> 00:07:26.870
Yeah?

00:07:27.420 --> 00:07:29.380
No, nothing.

00:07:30.360 --> 00:07:31.290
Oh...

00:07:35.390 --> 00:07:36.260
What?

00:07:36.260 --> 00:07:38.700
Oh, I'm here to pray for my entrance exams.

00:07:38.700 --> 00:07:39.880
Job search for me.

00:07:39.880 --> 00:07:41.820
I wanted to see the horse-shaped ema.

00:07:41.820 --> 00:07:43.370
I was bored.

00:07:44.280 --> 00:07:45.990
They're really shaped like horses!

00:07:45.990 --> 00:07:47.230
So cute!

00:07:47.230 --> 00:07:51.200
They're shaped like Banba 
horses... feels very local.

00:07:51.860 --> 00:07:53.410
<i>Crap...</i>

00:07:53.910 --> 00:07:57.620
<i>I don't really have any 
wishes to write down!</i>

00:07:59.080 --> 00:08:01.140
<i>I don't have any dreams for the future.</i>

00:08:01.140 --> 00:08:03.480
<i>Asking for something feels greedy.</i>

00:08:03.480 --> 00:08:07.100
<i>But it'd be stupid to write 
that I want to be with Mikage.</i>

00:08:07.100 --> 00:08:09.450
<i>Maybe I should just write down good health...</i>

00:08:09.450 --> 00:08:11.800
<i>but that makes me feel old.</i>

00:08:11.800 --> 00:08:12.960
What'd you write?

00:08:12.960 --> 00:08:14.970
Victory at the next competition.

00:08:15.250 --> 00:08:18.440
I see. I wonder what I'll put down.

00:08:20.370 --> 00:08:22.600
What'd you write, Hachiken-kun?

00:08:22.600 --> 00:08:24.270
Oh, what about you?

00:08:28.500 --> 00:08:32.770
Happy people should be blown to bits!

00:08:32.770 --> 00:08:35.450
Ookawa, they sell love charms.

00:08:37.410 --> 00:08:39.200
What'd you write, Aikawa?

00:08:39.410 --> 00:08:42.410
To become a vet, of course.

00:08:42.780 --> 00:08:45.670
Why are you trying to become 
one when you hate seeing blood?

00:08:45.670 --> 00:08:47.040
You've got the order wrong.

00:08:47.500 --> 00:08:50.000
I've always wanted to be a vet.

00:08:50.240 --> 00:08:52.820
But when I was in elementary school,

00:08:52.820 --> 00:08:55.330
I saw a really bad surgery on a cow,

00:08:55.330 --> 00:08:56.720
and it traumatized me.

00:08:56.720 --> 00:09:01.060
I see. So the dream came first, 
before you got the reality check.

00:09:01.060 --> 00:09:02.550
Yup, yup.

00:09:02.550 --> 00:09:04.970
I couldn't eat meat for a while...

00:09:05.710 --> 00:09:08.390
But I couldn't give up on my dream.

00:09:09.440 --> 00:09:11.620
I can't do anything about how I feel.

00:09:11.620 --> 00:09:15.340
It's not really about whether 
it's a good fit for me or not.

00:09:15.340 --> 00:09:16.000
Yeah.

00:09:16.950 --> 00:09:21.860
I bet that's what real dreams are like. 
You just <i>have</i> to do them.

00:09:23.430 --> 00:09:25.780
You and I are a lot alike.

00:09:26.550 --> 00:09:28.500
I liked studying from the start.

00:09:28.500 --> 00:09:30.630
But I got discouraged by reality.

00:09:31.330 --> 00:09:35.880
Even so, I recently realized 
that I still like studying.

00:09:36.920 --> 00:09:38.720
The difference between you and me

00:09:38.720 --> 00:09:42.630
is that I feel stuck and 
don't know what I want to be.

00:09:43.250 --> 00:09:45.890
Isn't it more fun to not 
think of it as being stuck

00:09:45.890 --> 00:09:48.730
and more as being free to be
 whatever you want to be?

00:09:50.180 --> 00:09:54.900
I'm so hard set on my one dream 
that there's no getting around it,

00:09:55.450 --> 00:10:00.800
but I think your dream's just wide open.

00:10:02.220 --> 00:10:03.260
There!

00:10:09.350 --> 00:10:12.130
<b>Ezonoo 

00:10:10.100 --> 00:10:11.330
Out!

00:10:13.610 --> 00:10:15.910
<i>There will be a player substitution.</i>

00:10:16.570 --> 00:10:22.700
<i>Ooezo Agricultural High School's pitcher is 
changing from Yamagoshi-kun to Komaba-kun.</i>

00:10:24.870 --> 00:10:31.440
Komaba!

00:10:29.580 --> 00:10:33.020
<b>May Ezonoo baseball club 
win the All-Hokkaido championships 
 Aki</b>

00:10:29.580 --> 00:10:33.020
<b>May the Ooezo Agricultural 
High School Baseball Club win 
 Hachiken Yuugo</b>

00:10:33.800 --> 00:10:36.020
<i>Four more wins, and we'll 
make it to nationals...</i>

00:10:36.940 --> 00:10:40.000
<i>Those four are a long haul...</i>

00:10:45.830 --> 00:10:48.830
<i>Wait, it's just four more.</i>

00:10:49.540 --> 00:10:51.170
<i>We </i>will<i> win!</i>

00:10:52.630 --> 00:10:53.690
All right!

00:10:57.150 --> 00:10:58.850
We worked so hard to make this,

00:10:58.850 --> 00:11:00.680
but the cleanup is so easy.

00:11:00.930 --> 00:11:02.320
That's just how it is.

00:11:02.320 --> 00:11:06.390
This is a field, and we promised 
we'd level it out again.

00:11:06.390 --> 00:11:08.250
Let's do it again next year.

00:11:08.250 --> 00:11:09.980
What? Again?!

00:11:09.980 --> 00:11:12.020
What? We weren't going to?

00:11:12.740 --> 00:11:14.490
<i>North Toukai's on the offense.</i>

00:11:14.490 --> 00:11:16.750
<i>In the batter's box is 
Kiyota-kun, number five.</i>

00:11:17.110 --> 00:11:18.890
<i>He's landed two hits so far today.</i>

00:11:18.890 --> 00:11:20.640
<i>On the mound is Komaba-kun.</i>

00:11:20.640 --> 00:11:21.610
Komaba?

00:11:21.610 --> 00:11:22.830
Icchan's pitching!

00:11:22.830 --> 00:11:23.660
Yeah!

00:11:24.600 --> 00:11:25.680
<i>We have a hit!</i>

00:11:26.380 --> 00:11:29.550
<i>First flyout, two outs!</i>

00:11:31.870 --> 00:11:33.600
<i>Toyohira-kun, number six, is up.</i>

00:11:33.600 --> 00:11:35.630
<i>First pitch is a strike! Low and away!</i>

00:11:35.630 --> 00:11:37.680
<i>Ooezo Agricultural High 
School's Komaba-kun's</i>

00:11:37.680 --> 00:11:39.190
<i>came in for the seventh inning,</i>

00:11:39.190 --> 00:11:42.300
<i>but he's holding the line 
with very few pitches.</i>

00:11:42.910 --> 00:11:44.510
<i>Fifth pitch coming up...</i>

00:11:45.230 --> 00:11:46.800
<i>Three strikes!</i>

00:11:46.800 --> 00:11:48.280
<i>It's over!</i>

00:11:48.280 --> 00:11:52.600
<i>Ooezo Agricultural High School wins 6 to 1!
 They will compete in the best eight!</i>

00:11:56.690 --> 00:11:59.320
In today's practicum, 
we'll make bridles for cows.

00:11:59.320 --> 00:12:05.230
Bridle

00:11:59.830 --> 00:12:01.830
See the handout for directions.

00:12:02.590 --> 00:12:05.240
You can make as many adult and 
calf-sized ones as you'd like.

00:12:05.970 --> 00:12:06.700
Begin!

00:12:08.090 --> 00:12:09.040
Like this?

00:12:09.320 --> 00:12:10.940
I'm a cow!

00:12:10.530 --> 00:12:14.070
<i>Ooezo Agricultural High School's on 
the offensive in the eighth inning...</i>

00:12:10.940 --> 00:12:11.890
A cow!

00:12:12.220 --> 00:12:14.070
Oof, we're losing 1 to 2.

00:12:14.070 --> 00:12:15.420
Sensei, we're in class.

00:12:16.090 --> 00:12:17.550
This is background music.

00:12:18.380 --> 00:12:20.050
Right on.

00:12:20.050 --> 00:12:21.860
Who're we up against in the second round?

00:12:21.860 --> 00:12:22.930
Daisetsuzan High?

00:12:22.930 --> 00:12:24.840
They're regulars at the nationals.

00:12:25.640 --> 00:12:26.640
There we go!

00:12:29.620 --> 00:12:32.220
<b>Ezonoo                                             Daisetsuzan</b>

00:12:29.710 --> 00:12:30.940
They took the lead!

00:12:30.940 --> 00:12:32.230
We can do it! We can do it!

00:12:36.270 --> 00:12:37.110
<b>Hiroo</b>

00:12:36.500 --> 00:12:40.540
<i>The pitcher is changing from 
Hiroo-kun to Komaba-kun.</i>

00:12:37.310 --> 00:12:38.270
<b>Komaba</b>

00:12:41.180 --> 00:12:42.150
Here we go!

00:12:42.150 --> 00:12:44.410
Komaba's totally a closer now.

00:12:45.890 --> 00:12:47.490
<i>Fly to center.</i>

00:12:48.280 --> 00:12:49.450
<i>Out.</i>

00:12:52.790 --> 00:12:53.910
<i>Strike!</i>

00:12:56.060 --> 00:12:57.380
<i>He couldn't hit it.</i>

00:12:59.210 --> 00:13:01.300
<i>Ball! 3-2 count!</i>

00:13:09.640 --> 00:13:11.390
<i>It's over!</i>

00:13:11.390 --> 00:13:14.540
<i>Ooezo Agricultural High School will 
go on to compete in the semi-finals!</i>

00:13:15.730 --> 00:13:17.000
We won...

00:13:17.000 --> 00:13:18.190
Wow.

00:13:18.610 --> 00:13:20.520
If we win two more times...

00:13:20.980 --> 00:13:22.650
We'll make it to the spring prelims.

00:13:23.260 --> 00:13:26.740
We really might get to cheer them on.

00:13:27.540 --> 00:13:31.430
What? They only managed 
to make this many bridles?

00:13:31.430 --> 00:13:34.160
Yeah, they're too slow.

00:13:39.570 --> 00:13:41.390
I'm back, Great-Gran!

00:13:41.900 --> 00:13:45.410
<i>We have Ooezo Agricultural High facing
Hakodate Ryuuhoku in the top of the first.</i>

00:13:45.410 --> 00:13:48.040
<i>Ezonoo's Hidaka-kun is up to bat.</i>

00:13:45.770 --> 00:13:47.310
You going to help—

00:13:48.040 --> 00:13:49.710
Oh, it's starting!

00:13:50.040 --> 00:13:51.640
Win this, Ichirou.

00:13:55.820 --> 00:13:57.350
Hello.

00:13:57.850 --> 00:14:00.620
Oh, why are you here, Headmaster?

00:14:00.620 --> 00:14:05.410
Oh, we have a few students 
in search of a TV...

00:14:05.950 --> 00:14:07.360
Are you using your monitor?

00:14:07.720 --> 00:14:11.070
Yes, I'm keeping tabs on 
cows about to give birth.

00:14:11.400 --> 00:14:14.310
We have cameras in the delivery 
room at the cattle shed

00:14:14.310 --> 00:14:17.040
and monitor them here.

00:14:17.750 --> 00:14:20.050
Can we watch baseball for a bit?

00:14:20.050 --> 00:14:21.850
Please!

00:14:21.850 --> 00:14:24.510
Oh, is today the semi-finals?

00:14:25.110 --> 00:14:27.970
<b>Ezonoo 
 Ryuuhoku</b>

00:14:25.800 --> 00:14:28.750
Crap, they've got three runs already.

00:14:28.750 --> 00:14:30.740
Is the other team strong?

00:14:30.740 --> 00:14:33.610
Yeah, they've made it 
to the nationals before.

00:14:34.050 --> 00:14:37.480
They let strong baseball athletes 
in from the Kansai region.

00:14:37.480 --> 00:14:40.020
Crap! They sound really strong.

00:14:41.310 --> 00:14:42.270
Safe!

00:14:42.530 --> 00:14:44.190
Great! Nice run.

00:14:45.150 --> 00:14:46.250
There we go!

00:14:46.250 --> 00:14:47.110
It's huge!

00:14:47.230 --> 00:14:49.420
<i>That's... not going to be enough!</i>

00:14:49.420 --> 00:14:50.610
<i>Ryuuhoku caught it in 
front of the right fence.</i>

00:14:50.610 --> 00:14:52.390
<i>Time to switch sides.</i>

00:14:52.390 --> 00:14:53.620
Aw, man...

00:14:54.080 --> 00:14:55.800
This is bad for your heart...

00:14:54.310 --> 00:14:56.810
<i>Ooezo Agricultural High 
School's second offensive</i>

00:14:55.800 --> 00:14:58.910
Wait, how're the cows doing?

00:14:56.810 --> 00:14:58.220
<i>ended without any points.</i>

00:14:59.470 --> 00:15:01.920
Oh! The calf's legs are coming out!

00:15:02.190 --> 00:15:02.790
All right!

00:15:02.790 --> 00:15:04.330
Let's go, Hachiken-kun!

00:15:04.330 --> 00:15:05.380
Why me?!

00:15:05.770 --> 00:15:07.230
No way, no way!

00:15:06.100 --> 00:15:08.680
You're the only one here 
who's in Dairy Science.

00:15:07.230 --> 00:15:08.180
I don't do deliveries!

00:15:08.180 --> 00:15:09.150
I'm not good at it!

00:15:09.150 --> 00:15:10.750
Please don't make me!

00:15:10.750 --> 00:15:13.480
We'll be sure to keep tabs on the game.

00:15:13.480 --> 00:15:15.390
No worries. Just go.

00:15:16.690 --> 00:15:19.980
It's okay to run away in order to live!

00:15:21.000 --> 00:15:22.890
<b>Calving Rope</b>

00:15:23.170 --> 00:15:26.610
No!

00:15:30.700 --> 00:15:31.590
Here.

00:15:35.270 --> 00:15:37.380
Milking the mom and giving the newborn calf

00:15:37.380 --> 00:15:39.530
his mom's milk is part of the process.

00:15:39.530 --> 00:15:43.830
Ugh, after giving birth, 
cows are stinky from sweat and blood.

00:15:43.830 --> 00:15:45.790
The milk makes everything sticky, too!

00:15:48.160 --> 00:15:49.700
Welcome back.

00:15:50.110 --> 00:15:50.920
Oh?

00:15:50.950 --> 00:15:53.000
<b>Ryuuhoku 

00:15:51.440 --> 00:15:53.010
We're winning?

00:15:53.010 --> 00:15:55.770
Well, they made some smart calls.

00:15:55.770 --> 00:15:58.470
Like how they put Abuta-san 
in as a pinch hitter...

00:15:58.860 --> 00:16:02.120
Cool how they dealt with it when 
the bases were loaded with no outs.

00:16:02.120 --> 00:16:04.200
That was really tense.

00:16:03.330 --> 00:16:06.360
<i>I feel like I got left out of 
the festival all over again...</i>

00:16:07.370 --> 00:16:08.950
<i>A short liner!</i>

00:16:10.180 --> 00:16:11.440
<i>Double play!</i>

00:16:11.440 --> 00:16:13.450
<i>Ooezo Agricultural High School 
couldn't add to their score.</i>

00:16:13.640 --> 00:16:14.960
Crap!

00:16:14.960 --> 00:16:16.550
Too bad!

00:16:16.550 --> 00:16:18.490
That was such a good chance.

00:16:16.550 --> 00:16:18.490
Let's see how the cows are doing.

00:16:19.630 --> 00:16:21.920
Oh, the next one's going into labor.

00:16:21.920 --> 00:16:23.680
Let's go, Hachiken-kun!

00:16:24.910 --> 00:16:28.050
No!

00:16:35.070 --> 00:16:36.050
Here.

00:16:37.370 --> 00:16:40.900
The previous cow had an 
afterbirth, so clean it up.

00:16:40.900 --> 00:16:41.830
Afterbirth?

00:16:42.220 --> 00:16:43.600
The stuff that comes out after a birth...

00:16:43.970 --> 00:16:45.270
The placenta.

00:16:45.270 --> 00:16:46.340
Ugh.

00:16:50.660 --> 00:16:51.730
Welcome back.

00:16:51.730 --> 00:16:54.070
Your joints are off, Hachiken.

00:16:54.380 --> 00:16:57.770
You must've gotten used to all of it after 
having to help with birthing twice in a row.

00:16:57.770 --> 00:16:59.260
I'm not used to it!

00:16:59.610 --> 00:17:01.300
I'm broken!

00:17:01.930 --> 00:17:04.070
Wait, how's the game going?

00:17:04.070 --> 00:17:06.020
We're winning 5 to 4.

00:17:06.020 --> 00:17:07.600
We're winning, but...

00:17:07.600 --> 00:17:08.220
Oh!

00:17:08.220 --> 00:17:08.750
<i>Ball!</i>

00:17:09.410 --> 00:17:10.710
<i>We've got a walk!</i>

00:17:10.730 --> 00:17:13.670
<b>Hakodate Ryuuhoku 
 Baseball Spirit</b>

00:17:11.130 --> 00:17:13.670
<i>We have bases loaded with no outs 
at the end of the ninth inning.</i>

00:17:14.030 --> 00:17:16.460
What? Are we in a tight spot?

00:17:15.510 --> 00:17:21.190
<i>Ooezo Agricultural High's changing 
pitchers from Hiroo-kun to Komaba-kun.</i>

00:17:17.140 --> 00:17:19.550
<b>Hiroo</b>

00:17:19.890 --> 00:17:20.600
<b>Komaba</b>

00:17:21.190 --> 00:17:22.410
Oh! Here he comes!

00:17:22.410 --> 00:17:23.850
Hang in there, Komaba!

00:17:24.130 --> 00:17:26.680
Crap, I'm super nervous.

00:17:26.680 --> 00:17:28.430
Bottom of the ninth with a one-run lead,

00:17:28.430 --> 00:17:30.000
bases loaded with no outs.

00:17:30.000 --> 00:17:31.900
I could totally die right now.

00:17:32.260 --> 00:17:33.070
Go for it!

00:17:38.720 --> 00:17:40.910
He's all in.

00:17:44.990 --> 00:17:46.170
Strike!

00:17:50.090 --> 00:17:54.100
Damn, that first-year 
sure knows how ta pitch.

00:17:54.100 --> 00:17:56.890
Quit it! Speak with a proper accent!

00:17:57.260 --> 00:17:58.680
No talking, please.

00:17:59.040 --> 00:18:00.490
Komaba's amazing.

00:18:00.490 --> 00:18:02.770
He's not intimidated by the other side at all.

00:18:02.770 --> 00:18:03.640
Yeah.

00:18:07.410 --> 00:18:08.770
Two more!

00:18:16.020 --> 00:18:16.890
<i>They caught it!</i>

00:18:16.890 --> 00:18:18.000
<i>The catcher got a fly ball.</i>

00:18:18.000 --> 00:18:19.030
<i>We're now at two outs.</i>

00:18:19.730 --> 00:18:20.990
One more.

00:18:21.460 --> 00:18:24.790
<i>We now have Iohara-kun, 
number four, third base.</i>

00:18:25.100 --> 00:18:27.720
<i>His batting average during the 
regional prelims was .632,</i>

00:18:27.720 --> 00:18:28.880
<i>with four home runs.</i>

00:18:28.880 --> 00:18:32.590
<i>In this competition, his batting average 
has been .527, with three home runs.</i>

00:18:32.860 --> 00:18:34.550
Who is this monster?

00:18:34.550 --> 00:18:35.930
Drop the third strike!

00:18:35.930 --> 00:18:36.990
Drop it, dammit!

00:18:36.990 --> 00:18:39.510
Even if he does, we'll still be 
even because they'll force an in.

00:18:39.510 --> 00:18:42.260
We just have to go for it.

00:18:42.680 --> 00:18:44.760
<i>Don't get intimidated, Komaba.</i>

00:18:44.760 --> 00:18:47.220
<i>If you do, the next throw 
will be the last one.</i>

00:18:48.630 --> 00:18:51.340
<i>Katou-san, right now...</i>

00:18:51.340 --> 00:18:54.960
<i>I think we'll win, even if I throw center!  {his mouth's op en here but i think it's still monologue}</i>

00:18:57.850 --> 00:19:00.530
We have a hit on the first pitch!

00:19:00.840 --> 00:19:02.240
Runners are all taking off!

00:19:05.720 --> 00:19:06.500
All right!

00:19:08.070 --> 00:19:09.430
A poor hit!

00:19:09.430 --> 00:19:10.540
Uryuu-kun's on the right field!

00:19:10.860 --> 00:19:12.260
If he can catch it...

00:19:27.070 --> 00:19:28.760
Game over!

00:20:01.120 --> 00:20:03.340
I'll... go to the cattle shed.

00:20:04.600 --> 00:20:06.550
I'll go check on the horses, too.

00:20:18.840 --> 00:20:23.750
I only got this far because 
you'd hit the ball

00:20:24.680 --> 00:20:27.440
whenever it counted, Uryuu-san.

00:20:31.390 --> 00:20:32.750
Thank you.

00:20:38.230 --> 00:20:43.680
<b>2013 66th Fall Hokkaido High School Baseball Championships</b>

00:20:39.200 --> 00:20:40.990
That was so close.

00:20:40.990 --> 00:20:42.390
Komaba was the key.

00:20:42.390 --> 00:20:43.680
He pitches like a gorilla.

00:20:44.010 --> 00:20:45.970
And here I was gonna have 
Hachiken show us around Sapporo

00:20:45.970 --> 00:20:48.170
if we'd made it to the finals.

00:20:48.170 --> 00:20:52.000
But it feels like we can even make 
it to the nationals next year.

00:20:52.000 --> 00:20:52.640
Yeah!

00:20:52.640 --> 00:20:54.640
Look forward to next year!

00:20:54.640 --> 00:20:57.860
Don't act so full of it when 
you're not even a bench player.

00:20:57.860 --> 00:21:00.680
I'm counting on Komaba.

00:21:01.040 --> 00:21:01.820
Huh?

00:21:01.970 --> 00:21:03.870
Is Komaba taking a break?

00:21:03.870 --> 00:21:05.450
Come to think of it, I haven't seen him.

00:21:05.700 --> 00:21:06.890
Did he catch a cold or something?

00:21:06.890 --> 00:21:09.140
Did he let go now that the tournament's over?

00:21:09.140 --> 00:21:11.570
I didn't know muscleheads 
could catch cold.

00:21:12.200 --> 00:21:14.160
<b>Go to Nationals</b>

00:21:14.160 --> 00:21:16.580
Dreams Are Infinite

00:21:14.160 --> 00:21:16.580
Full Sprint! 
 .           Full Pitching! 
.                   Everyone Do Baseball!!

00:22:45.690 --> 00:22:50.260
This story is a work of fiction.
